      textEn: 'The western section of Tuodong Road, near Desheng Bridge on the Panlong River, was once called Yunjin Street. It was an important ferry crossing on the river, where carriages, horses, and boats came and went incessantly. As night fell, the Yunjin Night Market came alive — vendors hawked their wares along the street, food stalls sent curls of steam into the air, and the aromas of tea and wine drifted on the river breeze. Lantern light reflected on the Panlong River, its rippling waters shimmering like starlight fallen from the sky. Old Kunming residents loved strolling through the night market after dinner: savoring a bowl of rice noodles, listening to a storyteller\'s tale, or gazing at the fishing lanterns flickering on the river. Yunjin Night Market was the most vibrant place in old Kunming, embodying the soul of street life and carrying the urban memories of generations. It was known far and wide as "Kunming\'s number one night market."',
