      title: '西街男孩洪泓的故事',
      titleEn: 'Hong Hong — A Native Son of West Street',
      text: '洪泓是土生土长的“老西街人”，成长于孝感巷口，日日望见开元寺东西塔，从小浸润在古城的历史传说之中。少年时代，他常在大榕树下听说书人讲述闽南典故，还主动登门拜访陈泗东等本地文史名家，埋下热爱本土文化的种子。2014年起，洪泓利用业余时间担任古城公益讲解员，化身当代“文化挖井人”，向游客讲述泉州的前世今生。他曾带领外国游客深度体验古城，将泉州“半城烟火半城仙”的生活样貌直播至海外平台；同时作为讲解员培训导师，不断学习更新知识，鼓励学员形成自己的讲解风格，致力于让世界读懂泉州千年海丝文化。',
      textEn: 'Hong Hong is a native of West Street. Growing up at Xiaogan Lane, he viewed the East-West Pagodas of Kaiyuan Temple every day and was immersed in ancient legends from childhood. As a teenager, he listened to storytellers under banyan trees and took the initiative to visit local cultural scholars including Chen Sidong, which planted in him a deep passion for Minnan culture. Since 2014, Hong Hong has worked as a volunteer cultural narrator in his spare time, acting as a modern-day "cultural well-digger" to share Quanzhou\'s past and present with visitors. He once guided foreign tourists for in-depth city experiences and streamed Quanzhou\'s unique lifestyle of "half mortal bustle, half immortal serenity" to overseas audiences. As a trainer for volunteer narrators, he keeps updating his knowledge and encourages trainees to develop their own narrating styles, devoting himself to introducing Quanzhou\'s millennia-old Maritime Silk Road culture to the world.',
