      text: '清明时节，泉州西街亚佛春饼老铺总是排起长队。傅锦娜是润饼皮制作技艺第四代传人。清光绪末年，傅家先祖傅维长习得润饼手艺沿街叫卖，后代在西街开设“亚佛”老店，传承至今已有百余年。润饼古称“春盘”，是闽南重要节令美食，如今被列入泉州非物质文化遗产。看似简单的薄饼，十分考验手感：面糊调配、火候把控、手腕力度全凭代代积累的经验。傅锦娜大学毕业后回到西街继承家业，坚守薄饼“薄如透光、柔韧不破”的标准。每到清明，海内外华侨专程前来购买润饼皮，一张薄薄润饼，裹着闽南春日风味，也承载着海外游子的浓浓乡愁。傅锦娜一边坚守传统，一边尝试创新，希望让这份泉州味道走向更远的地方。',
      textEn: 'During the Qingming Festival, long queues form in front of the Yafo Spring-Cake Shop on West Street. Fu Jinna is the fourth-generation inheritor of the runbing (soft spring-roll wrapper) craft. Back in the late Guangxu reign of the Qing Dynasty, Fu Weichang, the ancestor of the Fu family, learned the wrapper-making skill and sold snacks along the streets. Later his descendants founded the time-honored "Yafo" shop on West Street, carrying on the craft for more than a hundred years. Runbing, formerly known as Chunpan (spring plate), is a vital Minnan seasonal delicacy and is listed as Quanzhou intangible cultural heritage. Though it looks simple, making the thin wrapper demands consummate hand-skills: batter mixing, heat control and wrist strength rely on generations of accumulated experience. After graduating from university, Fu Jinna returned to West Street to take over the family business, sticking to the standard: wrappers shall be translucent, pliable and tear-resistant. Every Qingming, overseas Chinese travel far to buy the wrappers. This thin delicacy carries Minnan spring flavours as well as the homesickness of overseas compatriots. While preserving traditions, Fu Jinna keeps exploring innovations, hoping to bring authentic Quanzhou flavour to more people across the globe.',
